  "id": "mwd-lstm-sim",
  "stac_version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "## Overview\nThis collection contains EO project results from the **“Multisensor Water Discharges”** project, part of ESA’s Sentinel Users Preparation (SUP) initiative. The objective is to build representative, satellite-like datasets for future Copernicus Expansion mission **LSTM** to support the detection, monitoring and characterisation of water discharges in (a) inland freshwater near water treatment / sewage outlets and (b) coastal environments in the Adriatic and central Mediterranean. Data include simulated LSTM thermal stacks from Landsat/ASTER. Products are provided as STAC Items with assets in PRR Stagein S3 and are meant to be browsed via APEx / EarthCODE.\n\n## Data Sources\n- Landsat 8/9\n- ASTER\n\n## Spatial and Temporal Coverage\n- **Spatial coverage:** Italy\n- **Resolution:** 50 m\n- **Temporal coverage:** 2019–2025\n\n## Data Format\n- GeoTIFF\n- Coordinate reference system: EPSG:32633\n\n## Processing\nThese data are Top-of-Atmosphere TIR radiance.",
